## 1️⃣ TypeScript (Node / browser)

```ts
// src/Semaphore.ts

export class Semaphore {
  private _permits: number;
  private active = 0;

  constructor(private readonly slots: number) {
    this._permits = slots;
  }

  /** Acquire a permit – blocks until one is free. */
  async wait(): Promise<void> {
    while (this.active >= this._permits) {
      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0)); // tiny yield
    }
    this.active++;
  }

  /** Release the permit back to the pool. */
  release(): void {
    if (this.active > 0) {
      this.active--;
    }
  }
}

// ---- Example usage ----------------------------------------------------
(async () => {
  const limiter = new Semaphore(3); // allow up to 3 concurrent calls

  await limiter.wait();   // blocks until a slot frees
  console.log('First call in progress');

  await limiter.release();

  await limiter.wait();
})();
```

**Key points**

* `slots` is the number of concurrent permits.  
* `wait()` loops (with a tiny yield) until a permit becomes available; it then increments an internal counter (`active`).  
* `release()` decrements that counter when the operation finishes.

