## Summary of Design

| Feature | TypeScript | Python | Go |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Node structure** | `Map<string, TrieNode>` (dynamic) | dict-based (`{}`) | `map[rune]*Node` (Unicode-safe) |
| **`insert(word)`** | Iterates chars, creates nodes as needed, sets end flag. | Same loop logic with explicit map checks. | Creates child node if absent; walks to leaf and marks `isEndOfWord`. |
| **`search(word)`** | Returns `node.isEndOfWord` after traversing all chars or missing branch. | Traverses; returns boolean based on final flag. | Walks each rune; returns false on missing key, else checks end-of-word flag at leaf. |

All three implementations share the same algorithmic core: **O(L)** time per operation where *L* is word length, using a hash map for children to achieve O(1) average lookup per character.

