## How BFS Works (Unified)

| Step | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Queue** | Stores `(current_node, path_so_far)` pairs — FIFO ensures we explore neighbors level-by-level. |
| **Visited / Tracked nodes** | Prevent revisiting; the first time we hit `target` is via the shortest path (unweighted graph). |
| **Parent/Path tracking** | Append each neighbor to the current path when enqueuing, so reconstruction is trivial once target is found. |

All three implementations return a list of node labels from `start` → `target`, or `null` / `None` if unreachable.

