**Cosine similarity** between two embedding vectors \( \mathbf{a} \) and \( \mathbf{b} \) is defined as  

\[
\text{cosine\_sim}(a,b)=\frac{\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b}}{\|\mathbf{a}\|\;\|\mathbf{b}\|}
\]

where \(\cdot\) denotes the dot product and \(\|\cdot\|\) the Euclidean norm.  
